# Numbers Evolution - Cursor Rules

Project-specific development guidelines for Numbers Evolution - an educational Eurojackpot strategy testing application.

**Tech Stack:** Elixir, Phoenix Framework, Phoenix LiveView, PostgreSQL, OpenAI/Claude AI  
**Project Phase:** MVP Development (6-week timeline)  
**Developer Level:** Senior Elixir/Phoenix Developer

---

## Project Context

Numbers Evolution is an educational web application for testing Eurojackpot lottery number strategies through simulations. The application enables users to create strategies (manually or via AI), run parallel simulations on historical lottery data, and analyze effectiveness in real-time.

### Core Features
- User authentication and authorization
- Strategy CRUD with AI-powered generation
- Single and multi-simulations with real-time tracking
- Historical Eurojackpot data (100-200 draws)
- Strategy ranking and analysis
- Number proposal generator for upcoming draws

### Key Requirements
- Real-time simulation tracking via LiveView
- Concurrent simulations (3-10 parallel)
- Timeout limits (300s) and attempt limits (1M)
- Track only Grade I wins (5+2) in MVP
- AI rate limiting (5 generations/user/day)
- Template strategies as fallback

