### Real-time Simulation Tracking

**LiveView Pattern for Progress Updates:**

```elixir
defmodule NumbersEvolutionWeb.SimulationLive.Tracker do
  use NumbersEvolutionWeb, :live_view

  @impl true
  def mount(%{"id" => simulation_id}, _session, socket) do
    if connected?(socket) do
      # Subscribe to simulation updates
      Phoenix.PubSub.subscribe(NumbersEvolution.PubSub, "simulation:#{simulation_id}")
    end

    {:ok, load_simulation(socket, simulation_id)}
  end

  @impl true
  def handle_info({:simulation_update, %{attempts: attempts, progress: progress}}, socket) do
    socket =
      socket
      |> assign(:attempts, attempts)
      |> assign(:progress, progress)
      |> push_event("update-chart", %{attempts: attempts})

    {:noreply, socket}
  end

  @impl true
  def handle_info({:simulation_complete, result}, socket) do
    socket =
      socket
      |> put_flash(:info, "Simulation completed!")
      |> assign(:result, result)
      |> assign(:status, :complete)

    {:noreply, socket}
  end
end
```

### Form Handling

**Strategy Form with Changesets:**

```elixir
@impl true
def handle_event("validate", %{"strategy" => strategy_params}, socket) do
  changeset =
    socket.assigns.strategy
    |> Strategies.change_strategy(strategy_params)
    |> Map.put(:action, :validate)

  {:noreply, assign(socket, :changeset, changeset)}
end

@impl true
def handle_event("save", %{"strategy" => strategy_params}, socket) do
  case Strategies.create_strategy(socket.assigns.current_user, strategy_params) do
    {:ok, strategy} ->
      {:noreply,
       socket
       |> put_flash(:info, "Strategy created successfully")
       |> push_navigate(to: ~p"/strategies/#{strategy}")}

    {:error, %Ecto.Changeset{} = changeset} ->
      {:noreply, assign(socket, :changeset, changeset)}
  end
end
```

### State Management

- Use `assign/2` and `assign/3` for socket state
- Keep assigns minimal - only what the view needs
- Use temporary assigns for large data: `assign(socket, :large_list, temporary: true)`
- Debounce user input for AI generation: `phx-debounce="500"`

