## Common Pitfalls to Avoid

### LiveView

❌ **Don't** store large data in assigns:

```elixir
# BAD
{:noreply, assign(socket, :all_draws, Draws.all())}  # Could be thousands of records
```

✅ **Do** paginate and use temporary assigns:

```elixir
# GOOD
{:noreply, assign(socket, :draws, temporary: Draws.paginate(page: 1))}
```

### Database

❌ **Don't** forget to scope by user:

```elixir
# BAD - returns strategies from all users!
def get_strategy(id), do: Repo.get(Strategy, id)
```

✅ **Do** always scope:

```elixir
# GOOD
def get_strategy(user, id) do
  Repo.get_by(Strategy, id: id, user_id: user.id)
end
```

### Simulations

❌ **Don't** run simulations synchronously in LiveView:

```elixir
# BAD - blocks LiveView process
def handle_event("run_simulation", _, socket) do
  result = Simulations.run(strategy, draw)  # Takes seconds/minutes!
  {:noreply, assign(socket, :result, result)}
end
```

✅ **Do** use async processes:

```elixir
# GOOD
def handle_event("run_simulation", _, socket) do
  Task.start(fn ->
    result = Simulations.run(strategy, draw)
    send(socket.assigns.live_view_pid, {:simulation_complete, result})
  end)

  {:noreply, assign(socket, :running, true)}
end
```

### AI Integration

❌ **Don't** trust AI output blindly:

```elixir
# BAD
def generate_strategy(prompt) do
  response = call_ai_api(prompt)
  {:ok, Jason.decode!(response)}  # Can crash!
end
```

✅ **Do** validate and sanitize:

```elixir
# GOOD
def generate_strategy(prompt) do
  with {:ok, response} <- call_ai_api(prompt),
       {:ok, parsed} <- Jason.decode(response),
       :ok <- validate_rules(parsed) do
    {:ok, parsed}
  else
    _ -> {:error, :invalid_ai_response}
  end
end
```

